    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "@symnav/core\nScope → 6 handles",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "01\nSTATED\n↗\nCore owns lifetime; TypeScript owns meaning.\nOne scope per semantic service, with six isolated caches. The service still holds the scope instance. Algorithms, prepared source state and project logic stay where they were.\nThe spec assigns language-independent cache lifetime to core; the PR keeps six handles because their key and value spaces are independent.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "02\nSTATED\n↗\nKeep each answer’s identity and key space.\nFive caches hold promises by symbol identity; one holds locations by file + position. Hits preserve exact values and empty arrays. The generic core API also caches undefined. Reference projections and node arrays are rebuilt.\nThe PR explicitly preserves the existing algorithms, keys and identities. Map.has is chosen because undefined is a valid cached value.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "03\nSTATED\n↗\nOnly a successful refresh starts a turn.\nBoth versions clear after refresh succeeds, including an unchanged snapshot. A failed refresh leaves the current semantic cache entries available. This is a cache guarantee, not rollback of every refresh side effect.\nThe PR says failed refresh must preserve the current successful turn.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "04\nSTATED\n↗\nClear immediately. Then wait for project release.\nBoth versions clear first. The new service returns Promise<void> and the backend awaits it: pending release stays pending; an asynchronous project rejection reaches the backend caller.\nThe PR says released cache entries must be unavailable while release is pending or rejecting. It names the backend as the awaited release barrier.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "05\nSTATED\n↗\nKeep rejected promises; retry a factory that throws.\nA returned promise is cached even if it rejects. A synchronous throw occurs before insertion and can be retried. Clearing neither cancels an old promise nor lets its later settlement overwrite a new entry.\nThe PR explicitly preserves query failure behavior and promise identity; the added tests characterize both kinds of failure and old-promise settlement.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "06\nUNEXPLAINED\n↗\nExpose small, reusable handles.\nCore exports the scope and getOrCreate interface. Handles survive repeated clears; there is no public per-key invalidation, disposal, unregister, or lifecycle gate. The service keeps six for its lifetime.\nNo specific reason for this exact public API or handle-registration lifetime was found in the PR, commits or supplied spec.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "07\nUNEXPLAINED\n↗\nPass files instead of the whole snapshot.\nThe exported semantic service changes beginTurn(snapshot) to beginTurn(files: readonly WorkspaceFile[]). The backend passes snapshot.files; other snapshot fields no longer cross this method boundary.\nThe PR lists the signature change, but gives no reason for choosing this narrower input.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
    {
      "tag": "BUTTON",
      "text": "08\nSTATED\n↗\nAdd evidence around identity and lifecycle.\nSix semantic-service cases and four core cases are added. The five existing service cases and their assertions remain. No deleted or weakened existing assertions were found in this six-file diff.\nThe commits explicitly characterize semantic identities, specify the core lifecycle, and specify awaited semantic release.",
      "id": "",
      "href": null,
      "type": null
    },
